{
  "//": "Vintage Engineering's machines (mod id vinteng; checked against its 0.6.2 source, github.com/FlexibleGames/VintageEngineering). Each machine keeps its recipes in recipes/<machine> as plain JSON (ingredients, outputs, powerpercraft, attributes), which Vintage-E reads here so the mod's gears, concrete, wires, plastics, oil products and the rest get values. Vintage-E doesn't read these lists by itself, so nothing is superseded.",
  "//power": "Power: each recipe's powerpercraft, in Vintage Engineering's own power. Its LV generator makes 100 a second while charcoal (32 EMC) burns for 40 s, about 0.008 EMC a unit, but its solar panels and kinetic converter make power for nothing, and its big machines draw up to 15,000 a second. Priced at 0.008, a chemical plant on free power would turn 120 EMC a second into its outputs, so power is priced at 0.00005 instead: no machine makes more than 0.75 EMC a second from power alone, and values come almost entirely from the ingredients. A server can set its own price with EnergyEmc in /emc configure.",
  "//seconds": "A recipe takes powerpercraft / the machine's power a second (its block's maxpps): crusher, sawmill, press, extruder and mixer 100, log splitter 50, kiln 200 (and at least its requirestime), temporal forge 5000, distillation tower 2000, chemical plant 15000.",
  "//outputs": "An output's \"variable\" adds or takes off up to that many at random, so it counts as its stacksize. Liquids are given in litres. Codes without a domain are Vintage Engineering's, as in the mod.",
  "//tools": "The sawmill's blades, the press's molds and the extruder's dies are named by the recipe's \"requires\" and \"requiresvariants\" and lose 1 durability a craft, so a craft costs that share of the tool.",
  "//names": "Some mixer recipes name two inputs alike (the sand and the gravel of one rock): since Vintage-E 1.29.5 these are linked to the same variant, as in the game.",
  "format": 1,
  "requiresMod": "vinteng",
  "domain": "vinteng",
  "energyUnits": {
    "power": {
      "name": "Vintage Engineering power",
      "emcPerUnit": 5e-05
    }
  },
  "methods": [
    {
      "code": "vinteng:crusher",
      "name": "Crusher (Vintage Engineering)",
      "machine": "block:vinteng:vecrusher-*",
      "kind": "processing",
      "readers": [
        {
          "from": "assets",
          "folder": "recipes/vecrusher",
          "domain": "vinteng",
          "recipe": {
            "code": "$code",
            "enabled": "$enabled",
            "inputs": [
              {
                "each": "$ingredients",
                "code": "$code",
                "type": "$type",
                "quantity": "$quantity",
                "litres": "$litres",
                "name": "$name",
                "allowedVariants": "$allowedVariants",
                "skipVariants": "$skipVariants"
              }
            ],
            "outputs": [
              {
                "each": "$outputs",
                "code": "$code",
                "type": "$type",
                "quantity": "=default($stacksize, $quantity)",
                "litres": "$litres"
              }
            ],
            "costs": {
              "energy": {
                "unit": "vinteng:power",
                "amount": "$powerpercraft"
              },
              "seconds": "=$powerpercraft / 100"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
